            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I'd like a bit more of a \"why\" in the commit message. My understanding is we are doing this to support a redundant BMC environment in a situation where the active BMC is synching over data changes and we want the passive BMC to reload this data."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "Updated the commit message."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I'd like to see a few more tests.\n- Change a value in a persistent file, do the reload, and confirm the changed value from the file shows up on dbus and the service was correctly enabled/disabled\n- Send multiple reloads quickly and ensure they are queued as expected"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 26,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "I had tested these scenarios. Updating the commit message with the logs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/main.cpp",
                    "line": 360,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "This is all un-needed code if someone has not enabled the meson option, persist-settings-to-file, but it's also basically a noop if someone doesn't have the feature enabled. We'll see if anyone else weighs in on whether the signal handling should be wrapped behind that meson option."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/main.cpp",
                    "line": 360,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, I agree.\nThe `async_wait` where the signal is processed is wrapped in the meson option `persist-settings-to-file`. \nBut if the handling of signal is also wrapped, then when a reload is fired for `service-config-manager`, due to the changes made in service file to send a `SIGHUP` signal, it will execute it's default behavior - to terminate the service. The maximum tries to restart on termination is 3, after that the the service will be deactivated."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/main.cpp",
                    "line": 360,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "Updating to have the reloading of each unit wrapped based on the review comment [https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/service-config-manager/+/87981/comment/95695ee8_a6b2ffbb/] ."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/main.cpp",
                    "line": 360,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/main.cpp",
                    "line": 361,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: \"reload\" feels a bit vague. Maybe something more like \"SIGHUP signal handler for persistent data changes\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/main.cpp",
                    "line": 361,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/main.cpp",
                    "line": 366,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I think it's worth a comment to mention the fact that we're relying on the dbus event loop to queue and serialize additional signals here. Seeing a re-arm at the start of a signal handler is a bit unusual for me but I understand why from the commit message."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/main.cpp",
                    "line": 366,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, I have added a comment addressing this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/main.cpp",
                    "line": 380,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not sure if there's a situation where we could get this signal and \nthe srvMgrObjects may not all be available/valid but I think it's worth a \ncheck to ensure we've got a valid object before accessing it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/main.cpp",
                    "line": 380,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Riya Sabu",
                        "email": "riya.sabu461@gmail.com",
                        "username": "riya461"
                    },
                    "message": "I have included a check to continue the loop if the `srvObj` is valid."
                },
                {
